      "text": "Since $3$ and $-2$ are two roots of the equation, we can write the polynomial as $(x-3)(x+2) \\cdot \\frac{D(x)}{a},$ where $D(x)$ is the product of the remaining roots of the cubic equation. Since we don't know any more information about the roots of the cubic, we cannot easily find the value of $D(x).$ However, we can deduce that $\\frac{D(-2)}{a}=0$ and $\\frac{D(3)}{a}=18a.$\n\nMultiplying the trigonometric functions by a constant to make them integers, we have\n\\[\\boxed{\\frac{b+c}{a}=60}.\\]\n\nTwo roots are $3$ and $-2.$ So the roots are $3,-2,a.$ Thus the polynomial is by the roots is $x^2-11x+20,$ so the roots are $3,-2,5.$ Also by Vieta's theorem $b=-11$ and $c=20$ so we have $\\frac b a+\\frac c a$ which is $\\frac{-11+20} 5$.  Since they cancel out, we have $\\boxed{-1}$",
