      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let P(x) = a(x-3)(x+2) = ax^2 - x.\nThen the other root is r = P^-1(1) = P^-1(-P(r)) since P is one-to-one.\nBy going through all three steps repeatedly, we get the recurrence relation\n\\[P^{-1}(x)=x-ax-3+3a.\\]\nSince g(1) = 1, we have\n\\[\\frac{b+c}{a}=g(1)-2g(2)+3g(3)-a.\\]\nAlternatively, if P' is the derivative of P with respect to x, we have g'(1) = 1 and P'(1) = -a. The recurrence relation is therefore\n\\[g'(x)=-(x+r).\\]\nParsing this, we find\n\\[\\begin{aligned}\ng'(1) &= - (1 + r), \\\\\ng'(2) &= -(2 + 2a), \\\\\ng'(3) &= -(3 + 3a).\n\\end{aligned}\\]\nPlugging this in, we get\n\\[\\frac{b+c}{a} = -7 - a - 8a - 9a - 21a - 6a - 9 = \\boxed{-65}.\\]\nThe answer is: -65",
